---
import '../styles/components/about.css';
import '../styles/components/BrandPage.css';
import Icon from './Icon.astro';
import Related from './Related.astro';
import Logo from './Logo.astro';
import brand from '../data/brand.json';
import pages from '../data/pages.json';
import {Image} from 'astro:assets';
import board from '../assets/brand-board.png';
const page=pages.find(p=>p.slug==='brand')!;
---
<section class="page-hero wrap"><span class="eyebrow">THE TRACEGATE BRAND SYSTEM</span><h1>{page.headline}</h1><p>{page.summary}</p></section><section class="wrap"><div class="brand-cover"><div><Logo large/><h2>{brand.tagline}</h2></div><span class="meta">A cloud and identity security brand built around connected context.</span></div><Image class="brand-board" src={board} alt="Tracegate brand identity board featuring the orange gate mark, logo construction, palette, typography, stationery, and product applications." width={1500} format="webp" loading="lazy"/><p class="article-note">Art-directed identity concept board. Interface values shown in the board are illustrative. The implementation uses the downloadable vector mark and system documented below.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/brand/tracegate-mark.svg" download>Download the mark<Icon name="download" size={16}/></a><a class="button secondary" href="/brand/tracegate-wordmark.svg" download>Download the wordmark<Icon name="download" size={16}/></a><a class="text-link" href="/brand/brand-kit.json" download>Download brand tokens<Icon name="download" size={16}/></a></div></section>
<section class="section wrap"><div class="section-header"><h2>One idea, reduced to a mark.</h2><p>Two gates form a deliberate boundary. A diagonal signal path crosses the structure. The symbol expresses context becoming an intervention, without relying on a shield or a padlock.</p></div><div class="brand-cover"><Logo large/><p style="max-width:470px;font-size:14px">Leave clear space equal to the width of one gate stroke around the mark. Keep the geometry intact. Use signal orange on light or ink surfaces. The wordmark uses a compact sans-serif rhythm, and the mark can stand alone at small sizes.</p></div><div class="section-header"><h2>Color with a job to do.</h2><p>Signal orange identifies action and connected paths. Use the darker signal text token for readable small text on light backgrounds.</p></div><div class="swatch-grid">{brand.colors.map(c=><article class="swatch"><div class="swatch-color" style={`background:${c.hex}`}></div><div class="swatch-body"><h3>{c.name}</h3><span class="meta">{c.hex}</span><p>{c.role}</p></div></article>)}</div></section>
<section class="section-tint"><div class="section wrap"><h2>Technical clarity. Human readability.</h2><div class="type-grid"><div><h3>IBM Plex Sans Condensed · Display</h3><div class="type-specimen">See the path.</div><p>Use condensed semibold headings with deliberate spacing. IBM Plex Sans brings an open, readable rhythm to body copy and controls.</p></div><div><h3>IBM Plex Mono · Supporting</h3><div class="type-specimen mono">Aa 0123</div><p>Use for metadata, short technical labels, and supporting detail. Never make the whole marketing experience feel like a terminal.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section wrap"><div class="section-header"><h2>A voice that respects the operator.</h2><p>{brand.promise} Write with clarity, calm, and a specific mechanism behind every promise.</p></div><div class="voice-grid">{brand.voice.map(v=><article class="voice-item"><h3>{v.principle}</h3><span class="meta">SAY THIS</span><p class="do">{v.do}</p><span class="meta">AVOID THIS</span><p>{v.avoid}</p></article>)}</div></section><section class="section-tint"><div class="section wrap"><h2>Three messaging pillars.</h2><div class="value-grid">{brand.messaging.map(m=><article><h3>{m.pillar}</h3><p style="color:var(--text)">{m.message}</p><p>{m.proof}</p></article>)}</div></div></section><Related slugs={['about','platform','trust']}/>
